@fact pell.apothecary
# en: Runs the drawers at Pell & Daughters. He taught three generations of the village to count drops.
text [0b856c] = 管着佩尔父女药铺的抽屉。他教会了村里三代人数药滴。

@fact pell.counting
# en: He makes every new clerk count aloud. He trusts people who measure twice.
text [4c5e9c] = 每个新店员都得被他逼着大声数数。他信得过量两遍的人。
# en: Count with him.
hint [8ac258] = 陪他一起数。

@fact pell.daughters
# en: His daughters run the counter and want the shop to change; he wants it to be fifty years ago. They're all secretly proud of each other.
text [4a27be] = 女儿们管柜台，想让铺子变一变；他却希望一切停在五十年前。其实三个人都暗暗以彼此为傲。
# en: Meet the daughters behind the counter.
hint [37802b] = 见见柜台后面那两个女儿。

@fact pell.spoon
# en: His brass measuring spoon hasn't been wrong in forty years. His daughters learned to measure on it, and say it's theirs.
text [dc3a46] = 他那把黄铜量勺四十年没出过错。他的女儿们是用它学会量药的，她们说勺子是她们的。
# en: Ask about the brass spoon.
hint [b88cb2] = 问问那把黄铜量勺。

@fact pell.oldest_drawer
# en: His oldest drawer holds a yellowed card for a draught "of your own strength", in a hand older than his. He has labelled it "Not yet."
text [72e03f] = 他最老的那个抽屉里放着一张发黄的卡片，是一种“以己之力”的药剂，字迹比他的还要古老。他给它贴的标签是“还不行。”
# en: Restock the bottom of his wall.
hint [bf9dc7] = 去补他那面墙最底下的货。

@fact pell.humming
# en: Some of his thousand drawers hum. He relabels them himself, in a precise hand: ASK FIRST, NOT TODAY.
text [924948] = 他那上千个抽屉里有些会嗡嗡响。他亲自用一手工整的字给它们重贴标签：先问、今天不行。
# en: Listen to his drawers.
hint [e85071] = 听听他的抽屉。
